cartierInd -- computes the Cartier index
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = cartierInd E
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        (ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
  * Outputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, Cartier index of E
  * Consequences:
      * The result of cartierInd will be stored as a cacheValue (missing
        documentation) in E.cache#cartierInd.

Description
===========

Contrary to what the name suggests, *note ToricVectorBundle:
(ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundle, may well encode a toric reflexive sheaf
that is not locally free. cartierInd computes the Cartier index, that is, the
smallest non-negative integer i such that the pullback of the bundle under the
i-th toric Frobenius becomes locally free. In case of the reflexive sheaf of a
Weil divisor D, this is the smallest i such that iD is Cartier. This method
works well only on simplicial toric varieties.
cartierInd calls internally the method *note toricChernCharacter:
toricChernCharacter,.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P112 = ccRefinement transpose matrix {{1,0},{0,1},{-1,-2}};             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = {1,0,0};                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = toricVectorBundle(1, P112, toList(3: matrix{{1_QQ}}), apply( D, i-> |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|matrix{{-i}}));                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : details L                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = HashTable{| -1 | => (| 1 |, | -1 |)}                                    |
|               | -2 |                                                        |
|               | 0 | => (| 1 |, 0)                                           |
|               | 1 |                                                         |
|               | 1 | => (| 1 |, 0)                                           |
|               | 0 |                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : HashTable                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : cI = cartierInd L                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 2                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isLocallyFree L                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : L2 = toricVectorBundle(1, P112, toList(3: matrix{{1_QQ}}), apply( cI*D, |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|i-> matrix{{-i}}));                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isLocallyFree L2                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method works for a toric reflexive sheaf, which is locally Weil (see *note
isLocallyWeil: isLocallyWeil,),  on a toric variety, whose fan is covered by
cones of maximal dimension.

See also
========

  * *note ToricVectorBundleKlyachko:
    (ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundleKlyachko, -- the class of all toric
    vector bundles in Klyachko's description
  * *note toricChernCharacter: toricChernCharacter, -- computes the toric Chern
    character of a toric vector bundle

