compatibleBases -- computes compatible bases for a toric vector bundle
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = compatibleBases E
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        (ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, whose keys are maximal
        cones and the value of a key is a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)matrix,
  * Consequences:
      * The result of compatibleBases will be stored as a cacheValue (missing
        documentation) in E.cache#compatibleBases. It will be used by other
        methods.

Description
===========

Given a toric vector bundle in Klyachko's description, compatibleBases computes
for each maximal cone of the underlying toric variety a compatible basis of the
filtrations, see [RJS, Section 3] for details.
compatibleBases calls internally the method *note groundSet: groundSet,.


The compatible bases serve as input for the computation of the toric Chern
character by *note toricChernCharacter: toricChernCharacter,.

Caveat
======

This method works for any toric reflexive sheaf (see *note isLocallyWeil:
isLocallyWeil, for an example where the sheaf is not locally free) on a toric
variety, whose fan is covered by cones of maximal dimension.

See also
========

  * *note ToricVectorBundleKlyachko:
    (ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundleKlyachko, -- the class of all toric
    vector bundles in Klyachko's description
  * *note groundSet: groundSet, -- computes the ground set of a matroid
    associated to a toric vector bundle
  * *note toricChernCharacter: toricChernCharacter, -- computes the toric Chern
    character of a toric vector bundle

Ways to use compatibleBases:
============================

  * "compatibleBases(ToricVectorBundleKlyachko)"

