wellformedBundleFiltrations -- produces the same toric vector bundle, but where the filtration steps are stored in matrices with ascending entries.
***************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = wellformedBundleFiltrations E
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        (ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note vector bundle on a toric variety (Klyachko's description):
        (ToricVectorBundles)ToricVectorBundleKlyachko,

Description
===========

A toric vector bundle in Klyachko's description as used in *note
ToricVectorBundles: (ToricVectorBundles)Top, is given by ascending filtrations.
Unfortunately, the filtration steps are not always stored in an ascending way
by certain methods, like *note dual(ToricVectorBundle):
(ToricVectorBundles)dual_lpToricVectorBundle_rp, or *note
tensor(ToricVectorBundle,ToricVectorBundle):
(ToricVectorBundles)tensor_lpToricVectorBundle_cmToricVectorBundle_rp, (and
maybe others). This may cause problems in some methods of
PositivityToricBundles, for example in *note toricChernCharacter:
toricChernCharacter,. This method ensures that the filtration steps are stored
in an ascending way and therefore, that the methods of this package can be used
safely.
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = tangentBundle projectiveSpaceFan 2                 |
|                                                            |
|o1 = {dimension of the variety => 2 }                       |
|      number of affine charts => 3                          |
|      number of rays => 3                                   |
|      rank of the vector bundle => 2                        |
|                                                            |
|o1 : ToricVectorBundleKlyachko                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = T ** (dual T)                                      |
